ceiver more events about the tenant’s users than it asked for. The read list goes back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as it was; an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"text":" (the receiver’s “none”) goes back as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"text":" and is never omitted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cut to the new ceiling.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" When ","type":"text"},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lowers ","type":"text"},{"code":"eventsAllowed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and does not name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"eventsRequested","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the requested list becomes the entries of the read list that are in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the new ","type":"text"},{"code":"eventsAllowed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in their order (a request outside the ceiling is ","type":"text"},{"code":"400","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"eventsRequested","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that ","type":"text"},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sets to anything other than what was read — a list, ","type":"text"},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (absent: a reset) — is sent as given: the server judges it. Setting it to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"very value that was read is the same as not naming it, and is cut like the rest. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differs from §32.2 read literally, which would send a value set to the one read as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"given (the server then answering ","type":"text"},{"code":"400","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it lies outside the new ceiling): here the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cut is applied instead, which is benign. To send the read list uncut, build the body","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput\/init(copying:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and edit it yourself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"expectedUpdatedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as read."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"updatedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" string of the stream you read, byte for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"byte — never parsed and rendered again, because the comparison is of the instant and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timestamp rounded to fewer fraction digits than the server stored does not match. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"update then lands only on the version you read, and a write made since (the receiver’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own included) answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"409","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"ConflictError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never retried): read again and decide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again. Setting it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is “none”: the key is left out of the body and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never sent, which replaces whatever is stored.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The header.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authorizationHeader"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cle